- **Session host ↔ what it writes:** `stand_session_quiet` proves the session library and the harness path write nothing of the screen — typed text, a stable id, an accessible name — to stdout, to stderr or into the state directory, whose listing is `session.sock` alone, and that nothing on that path reads `RUST_LOG`: its host is the re-run test binary, which installs no log sink, so the `RUST_LOG=trace` it is started with is inert.
 It does not cover a host that installs escher's sink; that host is covered by seven_guis' `host_log` — the real `escher-session` binary on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace`, its needles read from the stand booted in the test's own process (at least 15 stable ids asserted, 16 read; the CRUD row and label texts), both streams drained by a thread each from the spawn on, the session reached with `attach` under a 60 s bound (never `start`, which reads no stream), driven since 2026-10-10-driver-cli by three calls through the binary as a client — a `snapshot`, a `click` and a `type` of a sentinel — and stopped with `stop`: exit 0, empty stdout, no state directory, at least one stderr line, every stderr line carrying `service.name=seven_guis`, exactly one `command` span line per call, and no id, no name and no occurrence of the typed sentinel anywhere on stderr, under the `-p seven_guis` build and the workspace build, a failure printing a kind and a count only — seen red on the unfixed sink (16 of 16 id needles and 6 of 6 name needles in 1501 stderr lines) — and by `telemetry_drop`, which proves the sink writes nothing for a third-party target at any level, native and bridged, under a `RUST_LOG` directive naming it; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the binary's `mcp` role is covered by seven_guis' `mcp_log` — at `RUST_LOG=trace`, under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build, 0 typed-sentinel occurrences, 0 id needles and 0 name needles on stderr, one `tool_call` line per call with only its stated field names, and protocol lines only on stdout (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:51-266); since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot `host_log` and `mcp_log` also drive shots and read 0 occurrences of a shot's first 64 base64 characters on stderr at `trace`, under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:398-411;
 examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:141-154), and each also drives one `lint` and one `snapshot` part read — `host_log` seven calls and 7 command-span lines, `mcp_log` ten tool calls and 8 `command` lines — still reading 0 needles on stderr at `trace`; `host_log` holds 3 tests and `mcp_log` 2. A paged `part` read through the `escher-session` host's own sink stays unmeasured — the host boots only the four lean tasks and none pages — its measurement owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line (target: next); the in-process capture reads one (`stand_act_spans`, §1).
 By level, both sink-installing binaries read 0 ids and 0 names at the default level, `info`, `debug` and `trace` — the windowed stand by the evidence instrument on the dev host, not by a standing check; since 2026-10-14-quality-gates the windowed binary built with the workspace, on the host's display, a client's own stderr and the host on flows beyond the three CRUD commands are read by build and level too, 28 runs with 0 needles, by the same kind of instrument (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/evidence/stderr-by-level.md), and a recording session's clients are read by a standing check
 — seven_guis' `cfg(unix)` `a_recording_sessions_clients_log_nothing_of_it_at_trace` runs each client command as a process through `common::run` at `RUST_LOG=trace` — `start crud --record`, `type --id crud-name --text {SENTINEL}`, `snapshot`, `snapshot --part 1`, `lint` and `stop` — in the state directories `hl-client` and `hl-client-rec` under `CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`, guarded by `common::Started { dir, pid }`, and over all their stderr reads 0 id, 0 name, 0 sentinel, 0 recording-path and 0 `recorded_needles` occurrences under the `-p seven_guis` and the workspace build, compiled for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` too (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:42-132);
 typed text is measured on the session host's log since 2026-10-10-driver-cli — 0 occurrences of a typed sentinel at `trace`, as `host_log` above — and stays unmeasured on the windowed binary's; it was first measured in process, where `stand_act_spans` runs the driver's `type` with escher's sink installed over a capture and reads 0 occurrences of the typed text, 0 of 36 ids and 0 of 8 names; since 2026-10-19-session-recording `host_log` and `mcp_log` each also run a recording host and a recording `mcp` role at `RUST_LOG=trace` and read 0 of the recording needles (the kept check's names and its directory's name) on stderr, the span counts unchanged, the kept check living in the launcher's recording directory and the state directory still `session.sock` alone (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_session_quiet.rs:30-115; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:30-492; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:36-40; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:57-64; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_drop.rs:16-67; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_spans.rs:1-24; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md, the in-process capture at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md)
